IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 (Cth), with the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Regulations 2018
-- -- whether super must be paid for a worker, on what earnings, at what percentage, by when, into which fund, and what the
-- employer can be made to pay if it is late.
--
-- SEAT: the employee, and the worker who may be one under s 12. Every decision is phrased as that person would ask it: "Am I an
-- employee for super?", "Must super be paid for me on this payday?", "How much?", "By when must it reach my fund?", "Which fund
-- must it go to?". The Act addresses the employer (s 16A: the charge "is payable by the employer") and the Commissioner; each
-- such duty is encoded as what it means for the worker: what must be paid for them, by when, into which fund, what they must be
-- given (a standard choice form, s 32N; a notice of a shortfall, reg 18), and what the employer can be made to pay if it fails.
--
-- Provisions covered. Act: s 6(1) ("business day", "usual period", "extended usual period", "ordinary time earnings",
-- "part-time employee"), s 10A(1)-(3), (6), s 12, s 16A, s 16B, s 17A, s 17B, s 18C(1), (2) item 1, s 18D, s 19B, s 20A(1), (2),
-- s 20C, s 20D, s 32C(1)(a), (1A), (1B), (2)(a)-(c), (2A), s 32CA, s 32F(2), s 32N(2), s 32NA(1), (5), (11), s 32Q.
-- Regulations: reg 11 (kinds of employees excluded, including (f) "a part-time employee who is under 18"), reg 12(1)(a), (b),
-- (c), (f) (kinds of payments excluded), regs 13B-13D (reductions of the administrative uplift), reg 17A (the stapled fund),
-- reg 18(1), (2) (notice to the employee of a shortfall component), reg 21(3) (a fund taken to be nominated).
--
-- Edition: Act -- Compilation No. 78, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes amendments up to Act No. 57, 2025 (the Treasury Laws
-- Amendment (Payday Superannuation) Act 2025), register id C2026C00272, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A04402.txt. Regulations -- Compilation No. 8, compilation date 1 July 2026, includes
-- amendments F2026L00133 (register id F2026C00535), as deposited at
-- ../../../superannuation-guarantee-administration-regulations-2018/registers/source-bundle/F2018L01289.txt.
--
-- THIS EDITION IS THE PAYDAY SUPER TEXT. The endnotes record ss 11, 23, 27 and 28 as "rep No 57, 2025" and s 19 as "rs No 57,
-- 2025", commencing 1 July 2026; Part 4 of the Regulations was "rs F2026L00133" from the same day. The quarterly scheme and the
-- 9.5 to 11.5 per cent steps of the old s 19(2) are not in the deposited text, and the compilation in force before 1 July 2026 is
-- NOT deposited. INFERENCE (the application items of Act No. 57, 2025 are listed in the endnotes but not reproduced): the old text
-- governs a payday before 1 July 2026. So for a payday before that date the percentage, the due date and the main question return
-- an explicit "earlier compilation not deposited" value, and the amount question takes the old percentage as an input the asker
-- must supply, labelled as such. Who is an employee (s 12, last amended in 2006 by the endnotes) is answered for any date.
--
-- FORMULAS NOT IN THE DEPOSIT. The formulas in ss 10A(5), 17A(2), 18C(1), 18D(2) and 19A(2) were images and did not survive
-- conversion: the deposit has "equal to:" and then "where:". The forms used below for 17A(2), 18C(1) and 18D(2) are INFERENCES
-- from the words around them (s 17: "equal to a particular percentage of the payment"; ss 18C(1)(d), 18D(2)(d): contributions
-- applied so as not to make the result "less than nil"). The maximum contributions base (s 10A(5)) and the individual notional
-- earnings component (s 19A) are INPUTS.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: defined benefit schemes and benefit certificates (ss 6A, 6AA, 10, 18A(3), 20A(3), 20B, regs 5A-10); the
-- complying-fund presumption and its exceptions (ss 18A(2), 18B -- whether a contribution is an "eligible contribution" is asked);
-- issuing exemption certificates (ss 17C, 17D -- whether one is in force is asked); out-of-cycle earnings and exceptional
-- circumstances (s 18C(2) items 2-4, (3), (4), reg 13); the Commonwealth as employer (ss 5, 5A); international agreements (s 15C,
-- reg 12(1)(d)); reg 12(1)(e), (g)-(j) and reg 12(2), (3); anti-avoidance (s 30); the rest of Part 3A (unfunded public sector
-- schemes, successor funds, agreements and awards, ss 32C(3)-(9), 32FA-32J, 32P, 32R-32ZAB); assessments, collection, the s 59C
-- penalty, Part 8 beyond reg 18 and reg 21(3); records (s 79). The charge itself is imposed by the Superannuation Guarantee
-- Charge Act 1992, not read. Public holidays are an INPUT list.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the individual
-- to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test
-- pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act 1992 -- the employee`

§§ `helpers and the two regimes`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
      `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`not below nil` MEANS
    IF `a` LESS THAN 0 THEN 0 ELSE `a`

-- The endnotes: Act No. 57, 2025, "sch 1 (items 1-64, 181, 182, 184-189): 1 July 2026". Gloss: the day the Payday Super text took
-- effect. A payday (the "QE day", s 17A(1)) before it is, by INFERENCE, governed by the earlier compilation, not deposited.
`the day the Payday Super text took effect` MEANS Date 1 7 2026

DECLARE `Which text governs` IS ONE OF
    `the Payday Super text deposited here`
    `the earlier compilation, which is not deposited`

@export Which text of the Act governs super on my payday: the deposited Payday Super text, or the earlier compilation that is not deposited?
GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid you (the QE day)
GIVETH A `Which text governs`
`Which text governs super on my payday` MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL `the payday` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the day the Payday Super text took effect`
    THEN `the earlier compilation, which is not deposited`
    ELSE `the Payday Super text deposited here`

GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposited text governs` IF
    `Which text governs super on my payday` `the payday` EQUALS `the Payday Super text deposited here`

§§ `s 12 -- am I an employee`

-- s 12(1): "employee and employer have their ordinary meaning. However, ... subsections (2) to (11): (a) expand the meaning of
-- those terms; and (b) make particular provision to avoid doubt". (2) a person "entitled to payment for the performance of duties
-- as a member of the executive body ... of a body corporate is, in relation to those duties, an employee". (3) "If a person works
-- under a contract that is wholly or principally for the labour of the person, the person is an employee of the other party to
-- the contract." (4)-(7) members of Parliament and the Territory Legislative Assemblies. (8) a person "paid to perform or present
-- ... any music, play, dance, entertainment, sport, display or promotional activity", or to provide services in connection with
-- it, or for work on "any film, tape or disc or ... any television or radio broadcast". (9) public office holders and persons
-- "otherwise in the service of the Commonwealth, of a State or of a Territory", but not "as a member of a local government
-- council"; (9A), (10) a council member is not an employee unless covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the TAA 1953.
-- (11) "A person who is paid to do work wholly or principally of a domestic or private nature for not more than 30 hours per week
-- is not regarded as an employee in relation to that work."
--
-- Gloss: "employee" here is wider than in the Fair Work Act: a contractor whose contract is principally for their own labour is
-- one. Whether a contract is "wholly or principally" for labour is a judgement the Act does not define: asked as a fact. Nothing
-- in s 12 asks the worker's age, whether the work is casual, or whether the worker holds an ABN.
DECLARE `My engagement` HAS
    `I am an employee in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I work under a contract that is wholly or principally for my labour` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am paid as a director or other member of a company's governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a member of a Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am paid to perform or present entertainment, sport or promotion, or for services connected with it, or for work on a film, tape, disc or broadcast` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I hold a public office or am otherwise in government service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a local government councillor acting as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the work is wholly or principally domestic or private` IS A BOOLEAN
    `hours a week I am paid for that work` IS A NUMBER

@export Am I an employee of the person who pays me, for the purposes of the Superannuation Guarantee (Administration) Act (s 12)?
GIVEN `my engagement` IS A `My engagement` @desc How you are engaged and paid
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an employee for super` IF
    IF      `my engagement`'s `the work is wholly or principally domestic or private`
        AND `my engagement`'s `hours a week I am paid for that work` AT MOST 30
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE IF `my engagement`'s `I am a local government councillor acting as such`
         THEN `my engagement`'s `I am covered by s 12-45(1)(e) of Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953`
         ELSE     `my engagement`'s `I am an employee in the ordinary meaning of the word`
              OR  `my engagement`'s `I work under a contract that is wholly or principally for my labour`
              OR  `my engagement`'s `I am paid as a director or other member of a company's governing body`
              OR  `my engagement`'s `I am a member of a Parliament or a Territory Legislative Assembly`
              OR  `my engagement`'s `I am paid to perform or present entertainment, sport or promotion, or for services connected with it, or for work on a film, tape, disc or broadcast`
              OR  `my engagement`'s `I hold a public office or am otherwise in government service`

§§ `reg 11 and s 6(1) -- kinds of employee whose earnings are excluded`

-- s 10A(3)(b): qualifying earnings "do not include ... earnings ... to the extent that: (i) the person is an employee of a kind
-- prescribed by the regulations". Reg 11: "a person's qualifying earnings do not include earnings ... to the extent that the
-- person is an employee of any of the following kinds: (a)-(e) [senior executives and managers holding a Subclass 456, 400, 482
-- or 457 visa, on the conditions stated]; (f) a part-time employee who is under 18."
-- s 6(1): "part-time employee means a person who is employed to work not more than 30 hours per week."
-- Gloss: the under-18 rule. It turns on the hours the young person is EMPLOYED to work, not the hours worked in a given week; the
-- encoding asks for the former. The visa limbs (a)-(e) are asked as one fact.
DECLARE `About me` HAS
    `my age in years on the payday` IS A NUMBER
    `the hours a week I am employed to work` IS A NUMBER
    `I hold a visa and a senior position of a kind reg 11(a) to (e) describes` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for me and this employer on the payday` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I a part-time employee as the Act defines it (s 6(1): employed to work not more than 30 hours a week)?
GIVEN `about me` IS AN `About me` @desc Your age, your contracted hours and other facts about you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a part-time employee` IF
    `about me`'s `the hours a week I am employed to work` AT MOST 30

@export Are my earnings excluded from super because of the kind of employee I am (reg 11)?
GIVEN `about me` IS AN `About me` @desc Your age, your contracted hours and other facts about you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my pay excluded because of the kind of employee I am` IF
        `about me`'s `I hold a visa and a senior position of a kind reg 11(a) to (e) describes`
    OR  (`Am I a part-time employee` `about me` AND `about me`'s `my age in years on the payday` LESS THAN 18)

§§ `s 10A(1)-(3), s 6(1) and reg 12 -- what pay counts`

-- s 6(1): "ordinary time earnings, for a person, means all of the person's earnings as an employee made up of: (a) earnings in
-- respect of ordinary hours of work; and (b) earnings consisting of over-award payments, shift-loading or commission; other than a
-- lump sum payment of any of the following kinds made to the person on the termination of the person's employment: (c) a payment
-- in lieu of unused sick leave; (d) an unused annual leave payment, or unused long service leave payment".
-- s 10A(1): qualifying earnings are "(a) the person's ordinary time earnings; (b) all commissions ...; (c) all payments for the
-- performance of the person's duties as a member of the executive body ...; (d) all payments under a contract referred to in
-- subsection 12(3) that are in respect of the person's labour under the contract; (e) ... remuneration ... as a member of the
-- Parliament ...; (f) all payments to the person for work referred to in subsection 12(8); (g) all remuneration ... in
-- circumstances referred to in subsection 12(9) or (10); (h) [salary sacrifice] an amount equal to the total of those
-- reductions." (2) an amount "is counted only once". (3)(a) not "the reversal of all or part of a sacrificed contribution".
-- Reg 12(1), for s 10A(3)(b)(iii): not "(a) payments to the person for a period of parental leave; (b) payments [by the usual
-- employer while the person is absent] where the person is engaged in an eligible community service activity; (c) payments ...
-- in respect of service ... with the Australian Defence Force ... by the person's usual employer while the person is absent ...
-- and ... not paid by the Australian Defence Force; ... (f) payments to the person that are fringe benefits".
-- Gloss: "qualifying earnings" is the base super is worked out on. Overtime is in none of the paragraphs: it is neither
-- "ordinary hours of work" nor "over-award payments, shift-loading or commission".
DECLARE `Kind of payment` IS ONE OF
    `earnings for ordinary hours`
    `an over-award payment`
    `a shift loading`
    `a commission`
    `overtime`
    `a termination lump sum in lieu of unused sick leave`
    `a termination lump sum for unused annual or long service leave`
    `directors' fees`
    `the labour part of a payment under a contract principally for my labour`
    `the part of such a payment that is not for my labour`
    `remuneration as a member of Parliament`
    `payment for entertainment, sport, promotion or broadcast work`
    `remuneration of a public office holder`
    `pay I gave up by salary sacrifice to super`
    `the reversal of a sacrificed contribution`
    `parental leave pay`
    `pay from my usual employer while I am away on eligible community service`
    `pay from my usual employer while I am away on Defence Force service`
    `a fringe benefit`

@export Is this kind of payment qualifying earnings, on which super is worked out (s 10A, reg 12)?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of payment` @desc What the payment was for
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this kind of payment qualifying earnings` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `overtime` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a termination lump sum in lieu of unused sick leave` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a termination lump sum for unused annual or long service leave` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the part of such a payment that is not for my labour` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the reversal of a sacrificed contribution` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `parental leave pay` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `pay from my usual employer while I am away on eligible community service` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `pay from my usual employer while I am away on Defence Force service` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a fringe benefit` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- One pay, in its parts. s 10A(4): "A payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee ... means: (a) a payment of qualifying
-- earnings to the employee ...; or (b) for qualifying earnings described by paragraph (1)(h)--the reductions".
DECLARE `My pay` HAS
    `the day I was paid` IS A DATE
    `ordinary hours pay` IS A NUMBER
    `over-award pay` IS A NUMBER
    `shift loading pay` IS A NUMBER
    `commission pay` IS A NUMBER
    `pay for my labour under a contract principally for my labour` IS A NUMBER
    `overtime pay` IS A NUMBER
    `termination leave lump sums` IS A NUMBER
    `salary sacrificed to super` IS A NUMBER
    `parental leave pay received` IS A NUMBER
    `fringe benefits received` IS A NUMBER
    `qualifying earnings already paid to me by this employer this financial year` IS A NUMBER

@export How much of this pay is qualifying earnings (s 10A, regs 11 and 12)?
GIVEN `about me` IS AN `About me` @desc Your age, your contracted hours and other facts about you
      `my pay` IS A `My pay` @desc This pay, in its parts
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my pay is qualifying earnings` MEANS
    IF `Is my pay excluded because of the kind of employee I am` `about me`
    THEN 0
    ELSE     `my pay`'s `ordinary hours pay`
        PLUS `my pay`'s `over-award pay`
        PLUS `my pay`'s `shift loading pay`
        PLUS `my pay`'s `commission pay`
        PLUS `my pay`'s `pay for my labour under a contract principally for my labour`
        PLUS `my pay`'s `salary sacrificed to super`

§§ `s 10A(6) and s 17B -- the maximum contributions base`

-- s 10A(6): if a payment "results in the employee's total qualifying earnings: (a) during the financial year; and (b) in relation
-- to the employer; exceeding the maximum contributions base, then treat the amount of that payment as if it were equal to: (c) if
-- that payment caused that total to exceed that base--so much of that payment as does not include the excess; or (d) if an earlier
-- payment had already caused that total to exceed that base--nil."
-- s 17B: if "an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for the employee ... treat the employee as having already
-- reached the maximum contributions base before the QE day."
-- Gloss: the cap on earnings super must be paid on, per employer, per financial year. Its formula (s 10A(5)) is not in the
-- deposit: an INPUT.
GIVEN `earlier this year` IS A NUMBER
      `this payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum contributions base` IS A NUMBER
      `a certificate is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment as counted` MEANS
    IF `a certificate is in force` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `earlier this year` AT LEAST `the maximum contributions base` THEN 0
         ELSE `the lesser of` `this payment` (`the maximum contributions base` MINUS `earlier this year`)

§§ `s 17A -- the percentage and the individual superannuation guarantee amount`

-- s 17A(1): "This Subdivision applies if an employer makes a payment of qualifying earnings to or for an employee on a particular
-- day (the QE day)." (2): "On the QE day, the employer has an individual superannuation guarantee amount for the employee equal
-- to: [formula not in the deposit] where: amount of the qualifying earnings means: (a) if there is one such payment--the amount of
-- the payment; or (b) if there are 2 or more such payments--the sum ... charge percentage means 12."
-- Gloss: the "charge percentage" is the share of qualifying earnings that must go to super. The deposited text sets one figure,
-- 12, with no table of dates; the earlier steps are in the compilation that is not deposited.
-- INFERENCE: the formula is the amount of the qualifying earnings times the charge percentage over 100.
`the charge percentage` MEANS 12

DECLARE `Super percentage` IS ONE OF
    `per cent` HAS `the figure` IS A NUMBER
    `not answered: the earlier compilation is not deposited`

@export What percentage of my qualifying earnings must go to super for this payday (s 17A(2))?
GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid you (the QE day)
GIVETH A `Super percentage`
`What percentage of my pay must go to super` MEANS
    IF `the deposited text governs` `the payday`
    THEN `per cent` `the charge percentage`
    ELSE `not answered: the earlier compilation is not deposited`

DECLARE `Super answer` IS ONE OF
    `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`
    `no: I am not an employee for this Act`
    `no: my pay is excluded because of the kind of employee I am`
    `no: an exemption certificate covers me with this employer`
    `no: none of this pay is qualifying earnings`
    `yes: super must be paid on this pay`

@export Must super be paid for me on this pay (ss 12, 10A, 17A, 17B, reg 11)?
GIVEN `my engagement` IS A `My engagement` @desc How you are engaged and paid
      `about me` IS AN `About me` @desc Your age, your contracted hours and other facts about you
      `my pay` IS A `My pay` @desc This pay, in its parts
GIVETH A `Super answer`
`Must super be paid for me on this pay` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs` (`my pay`'s `the day I was paid`)))
            THEN `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`
        IF (NOT (`Am I an employee for super` `my engagement`))
            THEN `no: I am not an employee for this Act`
        IF `Is my pay excluded because of the kind of employee I am` `about me`
            THEN `no: my pay is excluded because of the kind of employee I am`
        IF `about me`'s `an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for me and this employer on the payday`
            THEN `no: an exemption certificate covers me with this employer`
        IF `How much of my pay is qualifying earnings` `about me` `my pay` EQUALS 0
            THEN `no: none of this pay is qualifying earnings`
        OTHERWISE `yes: super must be paid on this pay`

-- For a payday before 1 July 2026 the percentage is not in the deposit. The asker supplies it, and the answer is only as good as
-- that figure. For a payday from 1 July 2026 the supplied figure is ignored and 12 is used.
@export How much super must my employer pay for me on this pay (ss 10A(6), 17A, 17B)? For a payday before 1 July 2026 you must supply the old percentage, which is not in the deposited text.
GIVEN `my engagement` IS A `My engagement` @desc How you are engaged and paid
      `about me` IS AN `About me` @desc Your age, your contracted hours and other facts about you
      `my pay` IS A `My pay` @desc This pay, in its parts
      `the maximum contributions base` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum contributions base for this payment, in dollars (s 10A(5); its formula is not in the deposit)
      `the percentage in the earlier compilation` IS A NUMBER @desc ONLY for a payday before 1 July 2026: the percentage the earlier compilation (not deposited) set; ignored otherwise
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much super must my employer pay on this pay` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`Am I an employee for super` `my engagement`))
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the payment as counted`
             (`my pay`'s `qualifying earnings already paid to me by this employer this financial year`)
             (`How much of my pay is qualifying earnings` `about me` `my pay`)
             `the maximum contributions base`
             (`about me`'s `an employer shortfall exemption certificate is in force for me and this employer on the payday`)
         TIMES `the percentage` DIVIDED BY 100
    WHERE
        `the percentage` MEANS
            IF `the deposited text governs` (`my pay`'s `the day I was paid`)
            THEN `the charge percentage`
            ELSE `the percentage in the earlier compilation`

§§ `s 6(1) and s 18C -- by when super must reach my fund`

-- s 6(1): "business day means a day other than: (a) a Saturday or a Sunday; or (b) a day which is a public holiday for the whole
-- of: (i) any State; or (ii) the Australian Capital Territory; or (iii) the Northern Territory." "usual period, for a QE day ...
-- (a) starting on the QE day; and (b) ending on the seventh business day after the QE day." "extended usual period ... ending on
-- the 20th business day after the QE day."
-- s 18C(1)(c): a contribution counts if "received during ... (i) the usual period for the current QE day; or (ii) the 12-month
-- period ending on the day before the current QE day; or before the end of the latest day in any applicable items of the table".
-- (2) item 1: "the first eligible contribution made to a particular complying superannuation fund or RSA by the employer for the
-- benefit of the employee: (a) after the employee commenced (or recommenced) employment with the employer; or (b) after the
-- employer ceased making ... eligible contributions ... to another complying superannuation fund or RSA" -- "during the extended
-- usual period".
-- Gloss: super must reach the fund within seven business days of payday, or 20 for the first contribution to a new fund. A
-- holiday for the whole of any one State, the ACT or the NT is not a business day anywhere: the holidays are an INPUT list.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a listed holiday` MEANS
    CONSIDER `holidays`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN FALSE
    WHEN `h` FOLLOWED BY `rest` THEN DATE_SERIAL `h` EQUALS DATE_SERIAL `the day` OR `is a listed holiday` `the day` `rest`

-- daydate's `Weekday of` gives 0 for a Sunday and 6 for a Saturday.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a business day` IF
        `Weekday of` `the day` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `Weekday of` `the day` LESS THAN 6
    AND (NOT (`is a listed holiday` `the day` `holidays`))

GIVEN `from` IS A DATE
      `count` IS A NUMBER
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the business day after` MEANS
    IF `count` EQUALS 0 THEN `from`
    ELSE IF `is a business day` `next` `holidays`
         THEN `the business day after` `next` (`count` MINUS 1) `holidays`
         ELSE `the business day after` `next` `count` `holidays`
    WHERE
        `next` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `from` PLUS 1)

DECLARE `Due date answer` IS ONE OF
    `by the end of` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`

@export By what day must the super for this payday reach my fund (s 6(1) usual period and extended usual period, s 18C(2) item 1)?
GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid you (the QE day)
      `the first contribution to this fund since I started or my employer switched funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first contribution to this fund since you started (or restarted) with this employer, or since it stopped paying into another fund for you
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Public holidays for the whole of any State, the ACT or the NT
GIVETH A `Due date answer`
`By when must my super reach my fund` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs` `the payday`))
    THEN `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`
    ELSE IF `the first contribution to this fund since I started or my employer switched funds`
         THEN `by the end of` (`the business day after` `the payday` 20 `holidays`)
         ELSE `by the end of` (`the business day after` `the payday` 7 `holidays`)

DECLARE `On time answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `late`
    `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`

@export Did this contribution reach my fund in time to count for this payday (s 18C(1)(c), (2) item 1)?
GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid you (the QE day)
      `received on` IS A DATE @desc The day your fund received the contribution
      `the first contribution to this fund since I started or my employer switched funds` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first contribution to this fund since you started with this employer, or since it switched funds for you
      `holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Public holidays for the whole of any State, the ACT or the NT
GIVETH AN `On time answer`
`Did my super arrive in time for this payday` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs` `the payday`))
    THEN `not answered: the earlier compilation governs this payday and is not deposited`
    ELSE IF     DATE_SERIAL `received on` AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the payday` MINUS 365))
            AND DATE_SERIAL `received on` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the last day`
         THEN `in time`
         ELSE `late`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the first contribution to this fund since I started or my employer switched funds`
            THEN `the business day after` `the payday` 20 `holidays`
            ELSE `the business day after` `the payday` 7 `holidays`

§§ `ss 18C, 18D -- how much of my super is short`

-- s 18C(1): "An employer's individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall for an employee and a QE day is equal to: [formula
-- not in the deposit] where: eligible contributions relevant for the QE day means so much of each eligible contribution ... as
-- ... (d) does not cause the amount resulting from this subsection ... to be less than nil."
-- s 18D(1): the final shortfall is "(a) if the employer's individual base superannuation guarantee shortfall ... is nil--nil; or
-- (b) otherwise--equal to the amount in subsection (2)"; (2) [formula not in the deposit] counts contributions "received during
-- the late period", again not below nil. "late period" (s 6(1)) runs from the day after the last day a contribution could count
-- under s 18C(1) to the day before the assessment.
-- INFERENCE: each formula is the earlier amount less the contributions it names, not below nil.
@export How much of my super for this payday was not paid in time (s 18C(1), the individual base shortfall)?
GIVEN `the super due for the payday` IS A NUMBER @desc The individual superannuation guarantee amount for the payday, in dollars
      `contributions received in time` IS A NUMBER @desc Eligible contributions that reached your fund in time for this payday, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my super was not paid in time` MEANS
    `not below nil` (`the super due for the payday` MINUS `contributions received in time`)

@export How much of my super for this payday is still unpaid after late contributions (s 18D, the individual final shortfall)?
GIVEN `the base shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What was not paid in time, in dollars
      `contributions received late` IS A NUMBER @desc Eligible contributions received in the late period, before any assessment, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my super is still unpaid` MEANS
    IF `the base shortfall` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `not below nil` (`the base shortfall` MINUS `contributions received late`)

§§ `s 19B and regs 13B-13D -- the administrative uplift`

-- s 19B(1): "The employer's administrative uplift amount for the QE day is equal to 60% of the sum of: (a) the total of the
-- employer's individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls for the QE day; and (b) the total of the employer's individual
-- notional earnings components for the QE day." (2): "this amount may be reduced (but not below nil) in accordance with the
-- regulations."
-- Reg 13C(1): reduces the percentage "by 20% if, during the 24-month period ending on the QE day: (a) no Commissioner-initiated
-- assessment ... is in force on the QE day; and (b) no estimate under subsection 268-10(1) ... has been made"; (3) for a QE day
-- from 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2028 the period is treated as starting on 1 July 2026.
-- Reg 13D: if the employer lodges a voluntary disclosure statement "before the day an assessment ... is made", reduce by: item 1,
-- 40%, "before the end of the 30-day period starting on the QE day"; item 2, 35%, to "the end of the 60-day period"; item 3, 30%,
-- to "the end of the 120-day period"; item 4, 15%, "after the end of the 120-day period".
-- Gloss: the uplift is a penalty-like addition the employer pays, on top of what it failed to pay; owning up early cuts it, to
-- nothing at best (reg 13D, Example 1). Whether the reg 13C conditions hold is asked as a fact.
@export What percentage administrative uplift can my employer be charged on top of my unpaid super for this payday (s 19B, regs 13B-13D)?
GIVEN `the payday` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer paid you (the QE day)
      `no Commissioner-initiated assessment or estimate in the reg 13C period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether reg 13C applies: no Commissioner-initiated assessment in force and no estimate made in the 24 months to the payday (from 1 July 2026 at the earliest)
      `my employer lodged a voluntary disclosure before any assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer lodged a voluntary disclosure statement for the payday before an assessment was made
      `lodged on` IS A DATE @desc The day it lodged that statement (ignored if it did not)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What uplift percentage can my employer be charged` MEANS
    `not below nil` (60 MINUS `reg 13C reduction` MINUS `reg 13D reduction`)
    WHERE
        `reg 13C reduction` MEANS
            IF `no Commissioner-initiated assessment or estimate in the reg 13C period` THEN 20 ELSE 0
        `days after the payday` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `lodged on` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the payday`
        `reg 13D reduction` MEANS
            IF (NOT `my employer lodged a voluntary disclosure before any assessment`) THEN 0
            ELSE BRANCH IF `days after the payday` LESS THAN 30 THEN 40
                        IF `days after the payday` LESS THAN 60 THEN 35
                        IF `days after the payday` LESS THAN 120 THEN 30
                        OTHERWISE 15

§§ `ss 20A, 20C, 20D -- the choice loading`

-- s 20A(1): the choice loading is "(a) if subsection (2) or (3) applies to some or all of those eligible contributions--the lower
-- of: (i) the amount equal to 25% of the total of the contributions to which that subsection applies; and (ii) the choice loading
-- limit for the QE day; or (b) otherwise--nil." (2) applies to contributions "not made in compliance with the choice of fund
-- requirements" where "(b) section 20D (relying on most recent Commissioner notification) does not apply".
-- s 20C(1): "The choice loading limit for the QE day ... is $1,200." (2): "reduced (but not below nil) by the amount equal to 25%
-- of the sum of any other eligible contributions" to which s 20A(2) or (3) applied "for any earlier QE day ... during the notice
-- period", which (3) begins no earlier than "1 July 2026".
-- Gloss: what the employer pays for putting my super in the wrong fund.
@export What can my employer be charged for paying my super for this payday into a fund that does not comply with my choice (ss 20A, 20C, 20D)?
GIVEN `non-complying contributions for the payday` IS A NUMBER @desc Contributions for this payday not made to a complying fund, in dollars
      `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period` IS A NUMBER @desc Such contributions for earlier paydays in the current notice period, in dollars
      `s 20D applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the stapled fund the Commissioner named refused the money and your employer paid it to another fund (s 20D)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What choice loading can my employer be charged` MEANS
    IF `s 20D applies` OR `non-complying contributions for the payday` EQUALS 0 THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of` (25 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `non-complying contributions for the payday`) `the limit`
    WHERE
        `the limit` MEANS `not below nil` (1200 MINUS 25 DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `earlier non-complying contributions in the notice period`)

§§ `ss 16A, 16B -- what my employer can be made to pay`

-- s 16A: "Superannuation guarantee charge imposed on an employer's superannuation guarantee shortfall for a QE day is payable by
-- the employer." s 16B(1): applies if the employer has "(a) one or more individual base superannuation guarantee shortfalls for a
-- QE day that are greater than nil; or (b) one or more choice loadings for a QE day that are greater than nil." (2): the shortfall
-- is "the sum of ... (a) the total of the employer's individual final superannuation guarantee shortfalls ...; (b) the total of
-- the employer's individual notional earnings components ...; (c) the employer's administrative uplift amount ...; (d) the total
-- of the employer's choice loadings". s 19: Subdivision D (notional earnings, uplift) "applies if an employer has an individual
-- base superannuation guarantee shortfall ... that is greater than nil".
-- Encoded for one employee and one payday. The notional earnings component (s 19A) is an INPUT.
@export In all, what can my employer be made to pay for my super for this payday (s 16B, the superannuation guarantee shortfall)?
GIVEN `the base shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What was not paid in time, in dollars
      `the final shortfall` IS A NUMBER @desc What is still unpaid after late contributions, in dollars
      `the notional earnings component` IS A NUMBER @desc The interest-like notional earnings on the shortfall (s 19A), in dollars
      `the uplift percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The administrative uplift percentage after reductions
      `the choice loading` IS A NUMBER @desc The choice loading, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What can my employer be made to pay for my super` MEANS
    IF `the base shortfall` GREATER THAN 0 OR `the choice loading` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN     `the final shortfall`
        PLUS `the notional earnings component`
        PLUS (IF `the base shortfall` GREATER THAN 0
              THEN `the uplift percentage` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES (`the final shortfall` PLUS `the notional earnings component`)
              ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the choice loading`
    ELSE 0

§§ `ss 32C, 32CA -- which fund my super must go to`

-- s 32C(1): compliant if made to "(a) a chosen fund for the employee". (1A): compliant if "(a) there is no chosen fund for the
-- employee; and (b) the most recent notification to the employer ... by the Commissioner ... is that the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that the fund is the stapled fund for the employee." (1B): (1A) does not apply while the employer "is required under section
-- 32N to give the employee a standard choice form; and ... has not done this by the time specified". (2): compliant if there is
-- no chosen fund, the Commissioner's most recent notification is "that there is no stapled fund for the employee", "(b) the fund
-- is an eligible choice fund for the employer", "(ba)" it is the fund the standard choice form names as the default, "(c) a class
-- of beneficial interest in the fund is a MySuper product", and (d), (e) the death-insurance requirements of reg 14 (folded into
-- one fact). (2A): (2) likewise does not apply while a standard choice form is overdue. s 32CA: "Despite section 32C", not
-- compliant "if the employer imposes a direct cost or charge on the employee as a consequence of having to contribute to that
-- fund."
-- Gloss: the order is my chosen fund; failing a choice, the stapled fund the Commissioner names; failing that, my employer's
-- default fund with a MySuper product. Other routes (s 32C(1)(b), (3)-(9)) are not encoded.
DECLARE `My fund facts` HAS
    `I have a chosen fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner's latest notice to my employer names a stapled fund for me` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner's latest notice to my employer says I have no stapled fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer is late giving me a standard choice form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer's default fund is an eligible choice fund with a MySuper product, meeting reg 14` IS A BOOLEAN
    `my employer charges me a direct cost for having to contribute to the fund` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Fund answer` IS ONE OF
    `my chosen fund`
    `the stapled fund the Commissioner named`
    `my employer's default fund named in my standard choice form`
    `no fund complies until my employer gives me a standard choice form`
    `no fund complies until the Commissioner tells my employer whether I have a stapled fund`
    `no fund complies while my employer charges me for the fund`

@export Into which fund must my employer pay my super for it to comply with the choice of fund requirements (ss 32C, 32CA)?
GIVEN `my fund facts` IS A `My fund facts` @desc Your choice of fund, the Commissioner's notice and your employer's default fund
GIVETH A `Fund answer`
`Which fund must my super go to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `my fund facts`'s `my employer charges me a direct cost for having to contribute to the fund`
            THEN `no fund complies while my employer charges me for the fund`
        IF `my fund facts`'s `I have a chosen fund`
            THEN `my chosen fund`
        IF `my fund facts`'s `my employer is late giving me a standard choice form`
            THEN `no fund complies until my employer gives me a standard choice form`
        IF `my fund facts`'s `the Commissioner's latest notice to my employer names a stapled fund for me`
            THEN `the stapled fund the Commissioner named`
        IF     `my fund facts`'s `the Commissioner's latest notice to my employer says I have no stapled fund`
           AND `my fund facts`'s `my employer's default fund is an eligible choice fund with a MySuper product, meeting reg 14`
            THEN `my employer's default fund named in my standard choice form`
        OTHERWISE `no fund complies until the Commissioner tells my employer whether I have a stapled fund`

§§ `s 32Q and reg 17A -- my stapled fund`

-- s 32Q: "A fund is the stapled fund, for an employee at a particular time, if the requirements prescribed by the regulations ...
-- are met". Reg 17A(2): the fund "(a) ... is a complying superannuation fund, or a complying superannuation scheme, for the
-- financial year ... or ... an RSA ...; (b) ... the employee is ... a member ...; (c) ... insofar as the Commissioner is aware,
-- that fund ... is able to accept contributions from the employee's employer; and (d) ... the Commissioner is able to disclose to
-- the employee's employer ... information". (1)(b), (3): if two or more funds meet (2), the fund is the one "(a) ... identified in
-- the most recent of those notices" given in the selection period; failing that, "(b) ... that received the most recent
-- contribution for the benefit of the employee during the selection period"; failing that, "(c) ... held the largest account
-- balance for the employee at the end of the previous financial year"; failing that, "(d) the Commissioner is satisfied that the
-- selected fund is the most appropriate". (4) the selection period runs from the start of the last completed financial year.
-- Gloss: the fund that follows me from job to job unless I choose another. Each limb is asked as a fact about this fund.
DECLARE `A fund of mine` HAS
    `it is a complying fund or scheme, or an RSA` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a member of it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as far as the Commissioner knows it can accept contributions from my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner can disclose the information to my employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `how many of my funds meet those four requirements` IS A NUMBER
    `a Commissioner's notice in the selection period named one of those funds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the fund named in the most recent such notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `one of those funds received a contribution for me in the selection period` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it received the most recent contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the balances at the end of last financial year single out one fund` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it held my largest balance at the end of last financial year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commissioner is satisfied it is the most appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Is this fund my stapled fund (s 32Q, reg 17A)?
GIVEN `the fund` IS A `A fund of mine` @desc Facts about the fund
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this fund my stapled fund` IF
        `the fund`'s `it is a complying fund or scheme, or an RSA`
    AND `the fund`'s `I am a member of it`
    AND `the fund`'s `as far as the Commissioner knows it can accept contributions from my employer`
    AND `the fund`'s `the Commissioner can disclose the information to my employer`
    AND (    `the fund`'s `how many of my funds meet those four requirements` AT MOST 1
         OR  (BRANCH
                IF `the fund`'s `a Commissioner's notice in the selection period named one of those funds`
                    THEN `the fund`'s `it is the fund named in the most recent such notice`
                IF `the fund`'s `one of those funds received a contribution for me in the selection period`
                    THEN `the fund`'s `it received the most recent contribution`
                IF `the fund`'s `the balances at the end of last financial year single out one fund`
                    THEN `the fund`'s `it held my largest balance at the end of last financial year`
                OTHERWISE `the fund`'s `the Commissioner is satisfied it is the most appropriate`))

§§ `ss 32F, 32N, 32NA -- choosing a fund and the standard choice form`

-- s 32F(2): "The fund becomes a chosen fund for the employee 2 months after the employee or the Commissioner gives the notice to
-- the employer, or at such earlier time after the notice is given as the employer determines."
@export By what day at the latest does the fund I chose become my chosen fund (s 32F(2))?
GIVEN `I gave notice on` IS A DATE @desc The day you (or the Commissioner) gave your employer notice of your choice
GIVETH A DATE
`When does my choice of fund take effect at the latest` MEANS
    `add months` `I gave notice on` 2

-- s 32N(2): "An employer must give a standard choice form to an employee within 28 days of the employee first commencing
-- employment with the employer." s 32NA: not required if "(1) the employee has chosen a fund under section 32F by the time
-- specified", "(5) the employee ceases to be an employee before the end of the period", or "(11) the employee is ... the holder
-- of a temporary visa". Gloss: the form that lets me choose my fund and names my employer's default.
@export Must my new employer give me a standard choice form (s 32N(2), s 32NA(1), (5), (11))?
GIVEN `I chose a fund within 28 days of starting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you chose a fund under s 32F within 28 days of starting
      `I left within 28 days of starting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you stopped being an employee within 28 days of starting
      `I hold a temporary visa` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a temporary visa under the Migration Act 1958
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my employer give me a standard choice form` IF
        (NOT `I chose a fund within 28 days of starting`)
    AND (NOT `I left within 28 days of starting`)
    AND (NOT `I hold a temporary visa`)

@export By what day must my new employer give me a standard choice form (s 32N(2))?
GIVEN `I started on` IS A DATE @desc The day you first started work with this employer
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my employer give me a standard choice form` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `I started on` PLUS 28)

§§ `regs 18 and 21 -- if the Commissioner collects unpaid super for me`

-- Reg 18(1): "The Commissioner must give written notice to an employee if the employee's shortfall component exceeds $20." (2):
-- "may give written notice ... if the employee's shortfall component is equal to or less than $20."
-- Gloss: the "shortfall component" is the part of the charge collected that is paid on for the employee (ss 64A, 64B).
@export Must the Commissioner tell me in writing about unpaid super collected for me (reg 18)?
GIVEN `my shortfall component` IS A NUMBER @desc The shortfall component for you, in dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must the Commissioner tell me about my shortfall component` IF
    `my shortfall component` GREATER THAN 20

-- Reg 21(3): "If a notice given under section 18 specifies a relevant fund, and the employee does not otherwise nominate another
-- relevant fund within 28 days after the date of the notice, the employee is taken ... to have nominated the relevant fund
-- specified in the notice."
@export Am I taken to have nominated the fund named in the Commissioner's notice (reg 21(3))?
GIVEN `the notice names a fund` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reg 18 notice named a fund
      `the notice is dated` IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today
      `I nominated another fund within 28 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you nominated another fund within 28 days after the notice
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have nominated the fund in the notice` IF
        `the notice names a fund`
    AND (NOT `I nominated another fund within 28 days`)
    AND DATE_SERIAL `today` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the notice is dated` PLUS 28
